From 1ccc1918fdb940f9b690284a9dc04327f04d2030 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:40:41 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(hints): scroll inside popover, compact card, side
 placement, first-occurrence marking

- scroll inside the popover no longer closes it (only page scroll does)
- find() and attach() share one lookup() rule so tests cover the real matching
- mark only the first occurrence of each card per theory page (print/for/if were underlined everywhere: 339 -> 122 tokens)
- place the popover to the right of the code block, then below/above it, so it does not cover the code being read
- compact card: example limited to 5 lines without blank lines, pitfall collapsed behind a toggle, no inner scroll
- close button on touch devices, aria-describedby on the active token
- tests: lookup() cases and find/lookup consistency (127 JS tests)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C7WzmRvdXnQ6c3tNNzhrtE
